export anchor ChatFirstStyle:
    number: 54
    screen: Inbox
    name: Chat-first
    idea: The inbox reads like a messaging app, with people as round avatars, notifications as speech bubbles and a composer bar always ready for a reply.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #e9f1ee, the pale green page behind the app
        panel: #ffffff, the app shell and message bubbles
        bubbleIn: #f1f4f3, the composer field and quiet tiles
        selected: #d8efe7, the open conversation in the list
        text: #14231f, body text, names and the active filter chip
        muted: #4f625c, previews, project names and times
        line: #d3e0db, dividers and bubble edges
        accent: #0b6e5f, the Reply button, outlined chips, links and the focus ring
        unread: #b5342a, the unread dot, the Unread word and the count badge
        mention: #4a1f78 text on #e7dcf3, the at name inside a message
    type:
        Segoe UI, system-ui, -apple-system, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
        sans-serif. The Inbox title is 24px bold. Names are 15px semibold,
        and 15px extra bold when unread. Bubble text is 15px on a 1.45 line
        height. Previews are 14px muted, and times, projects and badges are
        12px.
    layout:
        One rounded app shell 1240px wide at most. On the left a column
        380px wide holds the brand, Mara as a round avatar with an online
        dot, the Inbox title, the line 3 people are waiting on you, the
        filter chips and the conversation list. Each row has a 40px
        initials avatar, the name and time on one line, the preview below
        and the project with status words under it. The weekly report row
        uses a square chart tile in place of an avatar. On the right the
        open thread has a header with Priya, the task and project, a day
        pill, a centred context line, Priya's message bubble with her small
        avatar at its foot, the three option thumbnails as bubble cards,
        the time with Unread, then outlined chips for Mark as done and Open
        task. A composer bar at the bottom has an attach button, a round
        reply field and a pill Reply button. Below 820px the shell loses
        its corners and the list sits above the thread.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between bubbles and rows, 20 to 24px panel padding.
    density: Comfortable. Six conversations fill the list with room to spare.
    corners: 24px on the shell, 20px bubbles with a 6px tail corner at bottom left, 18px list rows, round avatars, chips, field and buttons.
    borders: 1px #d3e0db on bubbles and dividers, 1.5px accent on the outlined chips.
    shadows: The shell has 0 10px 30px rgba(11,60,50,0.12). Bubbles have a faint 0 1px 2px.
    icons:
        18px round line icons with a 2px stroke. People are initials
        avatars in six deep colours with white letters. Unread is a red
        dot with the word Unread, done is a tick with the word Done, the
        open row shows an eye with Open, and Mark as done uses a double
        tick.
    focus: A 3px accent outline offset 2px. A focused field gets an accent border and a soft 3px accent ring.
    tone: Conversational and warm, such as 3 people are waiting on you and Reply to Priya.
